# Never translate line endings, on any platform.
#
# This repository's evidence is byte-exact: conformance/wire-vectors.json is
# sealed by a digest, COMPONENTS.sha256 pins vendored trees by content, and
# live/epoch/testdata is compared byte-for-byte against its encoder. Git's
# default on Windows is core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout -- so the same commit produced different bytes there, the epoch
# vector comparison failed, and a second implementer verifying the corpus on
# Windows would have computed a different digest for it.
#
# A blanket rule rather than a list of extensions: the point is that a checkout
# is the commit, and an exception is a file where that stops being true.
* -text
